# WHAT THE IMAGE BUILD MUST NOT CARRY. `server/Dockerfile` does `COPY . .`, so everything here is
# sent to the daemon on every build; a checkout on a machine that has built once holds ~600 MB of
# `build/` directories, against ~28 MB of everything else. CI never noticed — a fresh checkout has
# none of them — which is exactly why this file is easy to forget and only bites locally.
#
# NOTHING GIT TRACKS MAY BE LISTED HERE, and that is not tidiness. The build context is a working
# tree as far as git is concerned: the `io.github.youndie.kore.build` plugin runs `git status` in it
# to decide the `dirty` flag it compiles into `/version`, and an excluded tracked file reads as a
# deleted one. The first published 0.8.0 image reported `commit: 8108f2f7f461-dirty` from a clean
# merge commit, because this file excluded `*.iml`, `kotlin-js-store/` and `**/node_modules/` — all
# three of which this repository tracks, `tailwind/node_modules` at 497 files. A flag that is always
# on is a flag that says nothing.
#
# So the list is only what git ignores anyway. `.git` IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT: without it the commit
# in `/version` is `unknown`, and it is 8 MB.
**/build/
.gradle/
.kotlin/
local.properties
